getTemplate -- construct the shifts and monomial partition for an elimination template
**************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        (sh, mp) = getTemplate E
  * Inputs:
      * E, an instance of the type *note EliminationTemplate:
        EliminationTemplate,,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Strategy => a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value null,
        the algorithm used to compute the template: "Greedy" (default),
        "Larsson", or null (standard GB)
      * AdjustParams => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value true, whether to run the greedy parameter-commit step (α-commit)
        for Martyushev's strategy
      * MonomialOrder => a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, default value
        null, override the default monomial order of the ring
  * Outputs:
      * sh, an instance of the type ShiftSet (missing documentation), a list of
        shift monomials applied to the generators of the ideal
      * mp, an instance of the type MonomialPartition (missing documentation),
        a list of three sets of monomials: {excess, residual, basis}

Description
===========

This method is the core of the *note EliminationTemplates: Top, pipeline. It
identifies the necessary polynomial shifts and partitions the resulting
monomial support into three blocks:

*   Excess: Monomials eliminated during the construction. *   Residual:
Monomials of the form $a \cdot b_i$ that are not in the basis. *   Basis: The
monomials spanning the quotient ring $R/I$.

If the action variable is a polynomial rather than a single variable, the
method automatically performs a lift to the graph ring $R[s] / \langle s - a
\rangle$.

+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x^2-y, y^2-x);                        |
|                                                     |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : E = eliminationTemplate(x, I);                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : (sh, mp) = getTemplate(E, Strategy => "Greedy");|
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : mp                                              |
|                                                     |
|        2     2    2                                 |
|o5 = {{y }, {x y, x }, {x*y, x, y, 1}}               |
|                                                     |
|o5 : MonomialPartition                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------+

